────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  COMPLEXITY TIER (issue #159)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Iteration 1 declared tier 1: single mechanism, single knob, treatment vs control
  Justification: iter 1, single mechanism (PD disaggregation), single knob (pd-decider), treatment vs control
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  SUMMARY
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  We are testing whether BLIS reproduces the core prediction from the prefill-decode disaggregation paper: that always-disaggregate (AD) mode lowers mean inter-token latency (ITL) but raises mean time-to-first-token (TTFT) compared to always-local (AL) mode, and that this ITL gap widens with increasing request arrival rate. This is iteration 1, Tier 1 complexity — a single treatment (AD) vs. control (AL) comparison across arrival rates.

  * Experiment: 2 × 13 × 3 = 78 runs. Two pd-decider settings (always vs never), 13 arrival rates (10–130 req/s in steps of 10), 3 random seeds each. Fixed workload: 300 requests, 512 prompt tokens, 128 output tokens, 4 instances (2 prefill + 2 decode), model qwen3-14b, trained-physics latency model.
  * Confirmation criteria: AD must show lower mean ITL AND higher mean TTFT than AL at every tested rate and seed. The ITL difference should grow with rate (consistent with 1/(1−ρ) nonlinearity). Both curves should be monotonically increasing and concave in rate.
  * Refutation signals: If AD does not lower ITL, investigate batch formation handling of decode sub-requests (IsDecodeSubRequest flag). If TTFT gap is absent, check KV transfer duration in metrics. If ITL-vs-rate is linear rather than concave, the utilization range may be too low to expose the nonlinearity — would need higher rates or fewer instances in a follow-up.
  * All unlocked parameters (max-num-scheduled-tokens=2048, max-num-running-reqs=256, pd-transfer-bandwidth=25 GB/s, etc.) are held at defaults with documented justification; none are confounds for this directional test.
  * Metric outputs go to per-run JSON files via --metrics-path; analysis will compare mean ITL and mean TTFT across arms, rates, and seeds.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

