  Iteration 1 confirmed all directional predictions: prefill-decode disaggregation (AD) consistently lowers inter-token latency (ITL) and raises time-to-first-token (TTFT) compared to always-local (AL) across all 7 arrival rates (10–130 req/s) and 3 seeds. The ITL gap widens from 0.13 ms at low load to 1.68 ms at high load, and the α/(1-ρ) formula fits both curves (R²=0.94 AL, 0.96 AD). The main open question is where the formula breaks down near saturation — rates above 130 req/s have not been tested.

