  This iteration (3 of a tier-3 escalation) tests whether a physics-corrected 3-parameter saturating model for inter-token latency (ITL) outperforms the paper's 2-parameter alpha/(1-rho) queueing model across 1–150 req/s, while simultaneously characterizing TTFT dose-response shape and the joint TTFT-vs-ITL tradeoff between aggregated (AL) and disaggregated (AD) serving modes. All three hypotheses share the same 72 simulation runs (2 modes × 12 rates × 3 seeds), estimated at ~3 minutes total wall time.

  * h-main: Fits a corrected saturating model ITL = a + b*rate/(1+d*rate) derived from batch-size-dependent overhead amortization in the simulator's step-time formula. Predicts higher R² and lower MAE than the paper's convex alpha/(1-rho) model for both AL and AD, with the paper model's MAE expected to be at least 2× worse due to systematic shape mismatch (convex vs concave data).
  * h-dose-response: Predicts TTFT follows a saturating (concave) curve for both modes, with AD's total TTFT growth across 1–150 req/s being less than one-third of AL's (~4.3ms vs ~15.6ms), because AD's dedicated prefill instances avoid decode-phase contention.
  * h-tradeoff: Predicts AD achieves lower end-to-end latency (E2E = TTFT + 127×ITL + overhead) than AL at ALL 12 tested rates, with E2E benefit growing monotonically from ~29ms at rate=1 to ~255ms at rate=150. The TTFT penalty (AD minus AL) is predicted to never exceed the 20ms budget, shrinking from ~15.7ms at rate=1 to ~4.4ms at rate=150.
  * Experiment: 72 runs of the BLIS simulator using qwen3-14b, 4 instances (2 prefill + 2 decode for AD), 300 requests each (512 prompt, 128 output tokens), pd-decider modes 'never' (AL) and 'always' (AD), 12 rates from 1–150 req/s, 3 seeds. No additional compute beyond what's needed for a single arm.
  * Confirmation criteria: (1) corrected model R² > paper model R² for both modes across all seeds, (2) TTFT shape is concave with AD growth < AL growth/3, (3) AD E2E < AL E2E at every rate and TTFT penalty < 20ms everywhere. Refutation diagnostics include checking seed variance, residual patterns at low rates, and whether a 4-parameter model adding queueing terms is needed.
  * Risk check: All parameters are pinned or use verified defaults; token budget (2048) comfortably exceeds per-request needs (640 tokens); no KV cache drops were observed at rate=150 in prior probes; the unlocked parameter audit is thorough.

